{"skill":{"slug":"antigravity-image-gen","displayName":"Antigravity Image Generator"},"version":{"version":"2.0.0","createdAt":1771355111026,"changelog":"antigravity-image-gen 2.0.0 includes metadata improvements and config clarifications.\n\n- Added .clawhub/origin.json and _meta.json for improved metadata and skill provenance.\n- Clarified authentication requirements and security note in documentation.\n- Updated config requirements to include auth.profiles in metadata.\n- No functional changes to the image generation process.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":".clawhub/origin.json","size":153,"sha256":"6ec6bb5255b1a14bc4ee8fc761fc9a448d3d1de2ab93792180e478856043fb15","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/generate.js","size":5794,"sha256":"38b7c69740370f7c7a1c2fb921ae2b895642342062fc81846343abc0713252f9","contentType":"application/x-javascript"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2040,"sha256":"f5fad7eebb1b3aac970334b8b3f7bef11ed01334bd8741dd1036383e646caa4d","contentType":null},{"path":"_meta.json","size":140,"sha256":"f3698dd84c5f37f84a0b3a0958be524dd26f814b759c0ac0e2dce27bfd3dc903","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2237,"sha256":"28b375d7f29a6ac6dfe31450c01446998a30c2ba4510ce62d7ef63e58f275c29","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789023844784,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5f1d41fd7bd6d05d6a37c77ec801194695b57c8c77e2a790483f36ffba9d849f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5f1d41fd7bd6d05d6a37c77ec801194695b57c8c77e2a790483f36ffba9d849f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: antigravity-image-gen\nVersion: 2.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its direct access and use of local OAuth tokens from `auth-profiles.json` (scripts/generate.js). While this behavior is explicitly declared in SKILL.md as necessary for interacting with an 'internal Google Antigravity API,' the capability to read sensitive credentials from the local filesystem is inherently high-risk. There is no evidence of malicious intent such as exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's behavior beyond its stated purpose. The network communication is solely with a Google sandbox domain.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160338962},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":80,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789023844784},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This image-generation skill is not clearly malicious, but it needs review because it uses local Google OAuth credentials with an internal API and spoofed client headers.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script reads the shared OpenClaw auth-profiles file, extracts a bearer token, sends prompts to a remote internal endpoint, and falls back to a hard-coded project ID if the profile lacks one.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package is small and transparent, with a Node script and no observed dependency installer, remote code retrieval, shell command execution, or install-time hook.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Activation is broad for ordinary image or visual-content requests, while the sensitive credential-backed provider choice is not gated by an explicit user confirmation in the skill instructions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, service installation, memory writing, destructive action, or local privilege escalation was found; the main privilege issue is use of an existing OAuth bearer token for outbound API calls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is image generation and the artifacts disclose local OAuth use, but the implementation calls a v1internal Google sandbox endpoint and intentionally presents Antigravity/Google tooling metadata rather than a skill-specific client identity.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable letting this skill read your local Google Antigravity OAuth profile, send your image prompts to the internal Google sandbox endpoint, and potentially use account or project quota under spoofed client metadata. Prefer a version that uses a documented API, an explicit project, and a dedicated least-privilege credential.","findings":"[PE3] expected: Authenticated image generation explains token use, and the skill discloses OAuth-token access, but reading a shared bearer token remains sensitive and should be tightly trusted.\n[LP3] unexpected: The artifacts disclose Node and auth-profile requirements, but they do not provide a narrow permission boundary or consent step for reading local auth material.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Broad triggers such as any visual-content request are not proportionate for a credential-backed internal provider and could invoke the skill unexpectedly.\n[SDI-2] expected: The local auth-profile read is part of the stated implementation, but it is broader than a dedicated least-privilege credential flow.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending the prompt and bearer token to the image service is functionally expected, but the skill lacks a runtime consent or clear endpoint warning at invocation time.\n[SDI-4] expected: The docstring/auth-source mismatch is minor because SKILL.md does disclose auth-profiles.json; this finding was downgraded in the final verdict.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The deliberate deprecation-bypass comment and fabricated client metadata are concrete under-disclosed behavior and a primary reason for Review.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding is supported by artifact evidence: the script uses an internal endpoint, spoofed client metadata, and a hard-coded fallback project, though it does not show exfiltration, persistence, or destructive behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789023844784}}}}}